From: Karu KVM integration fixture
Subject: [PATCH] RISC-V: KVM: refresh guest CSR configuration on debug changes

Pinned base: Linux 7.1.2 archive SHA-256
37198c93727be247c9fb5309bb86cd5e496c61e5322cd8c4eca9476bb0b5883f

The SET_GUEST_DEBUG callback updates guest_debug but never calls the existing
configuration helper. Disabling debug after the vCPU has run consequently
leaves breakpoint delegation disabled, and the same-vCPU load fast path can
retain stale hardware CSRs. Use the helper to update hedeleg and csr_dirty.
The unmodified RISC-V ebreak_test exercises this transition.

--- a/arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu.c
@@ -538,6 +538,7 @@ int kvm_arch_vcpu_ioctl_set_guest_debug(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu,
 	else
 		vcpu->guest_debug = 0;
 
+	kvm_riscv_vcpu_config_guest_debug(vcpu);
 	return 0;
 }
 
